# SQL migrations are embedded verbatim into the compiled binary via
# include_str!() and hashed by tauri-plugin-sql (sqlx) to detect drift —
# a line-ending-only change (LF vs CRLF, e.g. from core.autocrlf on
# Windows) flips that hash even though the SQL itself never changed,
# and the app refuses to start with "migration N was previously applied
# but has been modified". Pinning these to LF regardless of platform
# settings keeps that hash stable.
src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
